<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia says 95/96 coffee crop at 12.9 mln bags.</title>
<headline>Colombia says 95/96 coffee crop at 12.9 mln bags.</headline>
<dateline>CARTAGENA, Colombia 1996-11-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia produced 12.9 million 60-kg bags of coffee during the 1995-96 coffee year, the country's top industry official said on Saturday.</p>
<p>Jorge Cardenas, head of the powerful National Coffee Growers' Federation, said the figure of 12.9 million bags -- up slightly from previous estimates -- was now official for the coffee year that ended on September 30.</p>
<p>Cardenas, who spoke briefly to reporters on the sidelines of the annual National Exporters' Association meeting in this Caribbean resort city, declined to offer estimates for the 1996- 97 crop, saying it was too soon to make any reliable predictions.</p>
<p>-- Cartagena newsroom, (575) 665 0666, estension 1046</p>
